Since \(M\) is the midpoint of the arc \(AB\), and since the diameter is 6 cm, \(M\) is the midpoint of the diagonal \(AC\). This implies that \(M\) is the midpoint of the line segment from the center of the semicircle to the midpoint of \(AB\) in the case of a semicircle with diameter 6 cm (or \(M\) being one-third the length of the diameter over the radius, which is 3 cm).

Since \(AB\) is a segment of the radius of the semicircle, from the center of the semicircle to any point on the diameter (like \(M\)), the distance from \(M\) to \(AB\) is the length of \(AB\) divided by 2. We need to find the length of \(AB\).

