\[ (x - \sqrt{3})^2 + 2 = x^2 - 2\sqrt{3}x + 3 + 2 = x^2 - 2\sqrt{3}x + 5. \]
This expansion confirms the form of \( Q(x) \):
\[ Q(x) = x^2 - 2\sqrt{3}x + 5. \]

Now, we need to find \( Q(2) \). Substituting \( x = 2 \) into the polynomial:
